B2 is approved at artifacts.py SHA `135e006e892c6f32221d542bf5b9150c379d1a37713b3aa0e80307fe444174e1`. This supersedes the prior B2 corrections-required decision. Both findings are resolved; no additional actionable finding was identified in the correction diff and its shared append/replay call paths.

The authenticated author input is explicitly narrowed to AuthorRoleInputV5 and its complete hypothesis hash must match the durable intent before invalid identity derivation. Existing campaign/round, parent, template, assignment, discovery-plan and accepted-author checks remain in place.

Rejected hashes enter the set only after their context passes authentication. With no rejections, the new critic scan returns immediately. Otherwise every critic invocation is authenticated and checked regardless of acceptance or failure, and any bound rejected ID fails. Critics bound only to other candidates remain permitted by this check. The existing fold still rejects candidate work after critic completion. Both append and replay invoke the same validator; load_role_invocation does not recursively load round events.

Independent verification matched the source and preimage hashes, correction patch, actual06 inspection file, unchanged A/B1/B2 guards, and the 56-file evaluator identity `005064e57e80840f3b2a97d7db694b176832b8f982996e63efc8a35064505ed4`. Scoped Ruff, in-memory compilation and scoped diff checking passed. See `architect-verification.json` for the exact hashes.

