Next scope is B3a only: a separate rejected-candidate carrier and record construction, including optional-critic handling at that construction boundary. B3b will add record-to-journal authentication and publication safeguards. B4 will connect rendering, completion, recovery and subsequent feedback. The new B3a split is an architect scoping decision to keep each Luna review bounded, not a claim that all of B3 is ready.

Detailed next-session instructions are in `next-luna-prompt-b3a.md`. Return for architect review before B3b/B4. No production source, campaign, credentials, external calls, tests, candidate evaluations or deployment were touched during this architect review. The original two evaluated feedback rounds remain unfinished.
